course: dictionary
lesson: 8792
title: Shaped: having a certain form
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shaped means having a certain form, so a heart-shaped cookie has the form of a heart. The word is built from shape with -ed on the end, so the words around it tell you what the form is. «A field shaped like a square» means the field has the form of a square.
explain: Shaped can also be the past form of the verb shape, meaning to make something into a form. «She shaped the dough into balls» means she made the dough into balls. Check your meaning in the sentence: "she made the dough into balls" still makes sense, so shaped is the past of shape here.
explain: Look for a shape word before -shaped. In «a horseshoe-shaped scar» the hyphen joins horseshoe and shaped, so the scar has the form of a horseshoe. In «a ball-shaped nest», the nest is round like a ball.
fact: Shaped means having a certain form or outline.
fact: «Shaped» is also the past form of the verb «shape»: she shaped the dough.
fact: Put a shape word before -shaped to describe a thing: heart-shaped, star-shaped, L-shaped, ball-shaped.
fact: «Heart-shaped» on Pluto means the plain has the form of a heart.
fact: «Pear-shaped» can also mean gone wrong, but that is informal, so keep it for chatting, not for school writing.
exercise: «The wombat's droppings are cube-shaped and do not roll away.» What does cube-shaped mean? | *Having the form of a cube | Long and thin like a stick | Round like a ball | Soft and sticky
exercise: «She shaped the dough into balls.» What is shaped here? | A word that means very big | A type of hook | *The past form of shape: she made the dough into balls | A kind of cake
exercise: «The harvest mouse weaves a ball-shaped nest among tall grass.» What does the nest look like? | Square, like a box | Long, like a snake | Flat, like a pancake | *Round, like a ball
test: «Pluto turned out to have a heart-shaped plain of nitrogen ice.» Which word tells you the plain's form? | Pluto | lively | *heart-shaped | haze
test: Which word is the past form of shape in «He shaped the clay into a bowl»? | clay | *shaped | the | bowl
exam: In «a horseshoe-shaped scar», what does horseshoe-shaped mean? | Very shiny and new | Gone wrong, informal | *Having the form of a horseshoe | Hidden under leaves
